Date:     Fri, 24 Dec 93 9:45:32 GMT
From: nancy@genie.slhs.udel.edu
Subject:  subgroups for the list?

This is offered as quite a tentative suggestion, but I wonder if 
there's a practical way to set up subgroups for extropians.
Part of my reasoning is that a lot of people have left the list
because they don't want to handle the traffic, and part of it
is that while I've found that the quarrel with Tim May has been
educational, I'm feeling educated enough by it at the moment.

I'm not sure how difficult it would be to have a software solution
that would offer more than one subgroup--people would be free
to subscribe to as many as they waed. The division I'm
proposing would be between people who think that being offensive
is fun or useful, and those who don't. My impression is that
there are enough people on both sides that each group could
be self-sustaining. 

I certainly wouldn't want whoever's doing list justice to be
stuck with the work of "protecting" the groups from each other.
Do people think that (you should pardon the expression) "social
norms" could be strong enough to convince people to keep the
different approaches in different groups for the most part?

I'm not saying that this would be the only possible split
(though if it can be done, it might supply an interesting
experiment in the effects of the two communication styles),
but one of the things I've been mulling has been the effects
of the groups on the net getting unreadably large, and I'm
convinced that (until we've got some way of increasing our
input rate) there needs to be a graceful way of letting
groups divide into socially managable sizes.

Nancy Lebovitz 



